{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence iteratively.\n    This function avoids recursion and redundant calculations for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize a list to store computed Fib4 values.\n    memo = [0] * (n + 1)\n    memo[0] = 0\n    memo[1] = 0\n    memo[2] = 2\n    memo[3] = 0\n\n    # Calculate fib4(i) for i from 4 up to n using the recurrence relation.\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        memo[i] = memo[i-1] + memo[i-2] + memo[i-3] + memo[i-4]\n    \n    return memo[n]"}
