{"task_id": "HumanEval/96", "solution": "def count_up_to(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a list of all prime numbers strictly less than n using the Sieve of Eratosthenes.\n    Handles non-negative integer n, returning an empty list for n <= 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 2:\n        return []\n\n    # Initialize a boolean array where is_prime_sieve[i] is True if i is prime.\n    is_prime_sieve = [True] * n\n    is_prime_sieve[0] = False  # 0 is not prime\n    is_prime_sieve[1] = False  # 1 is not prime\n\n    p = 2\n    # Apply the Sieve of Eratosthenes algorithm.\n    while (p * p < n):\n        if is_prime_sieve[p]:\n            for i in range(p * p, n, p):\n                is_prime_sieve[i] = False\n        p += 1\n    \n    # Collect all numbers marked as prime into a list.\n    primes = []\n    for num in range(2, n):\n        if is_prime_sieve[num]:\n            primes.append(num)\n            \n    return primes"}
